* TOOL_CONFIG
* The configuration on one screen: every parameter of sd.conf with the value SD is running with, the value the file now says, the default, what the parameter does and when a change reaches
* anyone; the backup directory; and the operating system's part of the settings report (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md section 5, A6).  Since 26 Oct 26 it can change the
* 14 tuning parameters of the table's 'write' column, through SET.CONFIG and SDSYS's elevated helper.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux (S.75 A6 and its later changes to 9 Nov 26; RELEASE_1.1 218).  OS deviations: sd.conf is the file kernel(K$INIPATH) names (SD_CONFIG, else
*               C:\ProgramData\SD\sd.conf), not /etc/sd.conf; set.config changes it through SDSYS's elevated helper (gplbld/sd-confset.ps1), not the root helper; the line to add by hand is
*               added as an administrator; a restart is sd -restart, or Stop-Service SD and Start-Service SD; the report's operating-system part is Windows's (no sudoers file).
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the three boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): drawn exactly as before at 140 by 43, and in a larger window the parameter list takes the extra rows, every
*               box and text is as wide as the window, and the detail wraps at the box's width. The rows, widths, hit tests and the [?] button are counted from the pane rectangles.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.87: CLOSESEQ and EQU are gone as statements: this program says CLOSE and EQUATE.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  A file path too long for the top line loses its front ('...'), no longer the counts after it.
* 26 Oct 26 dm  A6, the write half (the owner: "do a6"): E on a parameter asks for a new value, checks it against the table, shows the exact set.config command and when it takes effect in the
*               toolkit's confirm box, runs it with $tk_run, and reads the file and SD's own values again; a parameter the table marks write=no shows why and the line to add by hand, and writes nothing.
*               The table gained its 'write' and 'why' fields and the page a Change column.
* 26 Oct 26 dm  read.table assigns every column by line number: an append with <-1> to a still-empty array adds nothing, so the minimum and maximum columns (blank for the table's first rows) slid
*               up and the foot box showed another parameter's range on the first rows (found by the write half's own check of the range E validates against).
* 27 Oct 26 dm  S.87 batch 15: no parameter is inert or retired any more (the eleven that were are gone from sd.conf), so the 'inert' sentence at the foot is gone; the other parameters number 37.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; the three views, the differ filter and refresh are offered to the model.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the view to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (the cases act:std.mouse and ctrl-o, through $tk_std).
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - the two sentences that name SDSYS's helper are double-quoted: a string ends at its own quote (op_str3.c, no ''
*               escape), so 'SDSYS''s ...' was two strings side by side; in SCREEN TEXT (line 565) that did not compile, and the cycle of
*               10 Nov 20:44 stopped at SECOND.COMPILE on it.  The EL<-1> sentence was made the same way and is changed with it.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.CONFIG      (SDSYS's VOC only; the audience is the administrator, asked of the kernel before anything is read)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least).  Everything it does by itself is LOOKING; its one way of changing anything is the command set.config,
*   which it runs only after the person has typed a value, the page has checked the value against the table's range, and the confirm box has shown the exact sentence and answered Run.
*   set.config calls SDSYS's elevated helper (gplbld/sd-confset.ps1), which changes one of 14 tuning parameters and refuses everything else; the page never writes a file and never runs anything else.
*   The other 37 parameters are not changed from here (the doors, paths and commands, logs and diagnostics, sizes config.c does not check, ...): E shows the reason, from the table, and the
*   line to add by hand.
*
*   Three views.  P, the parameters: one row for each parameter SD knows (the table sdsys/config.table, which test-toolconfig-units.py holds to the parser in config.c), with the value
*   the CONFIG function reports (what this SD is running with), the value sd.conf says now (the file read again, a parameter written twice counted the way SD counts it), the default, when
*   a change takes effect (session: a session reads sd.conf itself when it starts, so the sessions started after an edit see it; restart: it sizes or starts the system) and whether anything
*   acts on it.  A row marked * is one where the file and the running SD disagree; the box at the foot says who will see the file's value.  A name in the file that SD does not know
*   is listed as unknown and said to stop SD and every new session from starting, which it does.  B, the backup directory: the saved directory and whether it is there.  R, the
*   operating system's part of settings.report (the ssh and API doors, the groups, the service), read when the view is opened and on F5.
*
*   Keys: P, B, R change the view; Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End move; D shows only the rows where the file and SD disagree; S only the parameters the file sets; E changes the parameter
*   under the cursor (or says why it cannot be changed here); F5 reads the file and the report again; F1 or ? or a click on the [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.  A click on a row puts
*   the cursor there.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_config
$catalog $tool_config

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'set.config'                                         ;* the one command this page may run
   call $tk_open('tool.config', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.config')

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'p', 'parameters', 'parameters', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'b', 'backups', 'backups', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'r', 'report', 'report', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'differ', 'differ', 'Parameters', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 's', 'set', 'setonly', 'Parameters', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'e', 'change', 'edit', 'Parameters', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'read', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U3: Esc goes back to the parameters and takes the row filters off first, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'edit', '&Parameter', '&Change this parameter', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'parameters', '&View', '&Parameters', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'backups', '&View', '&Backup directory', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'report', '&View', '&Report', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'differ', '&View', '&Differences only', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'setonly', '&View', '&Set by the file only', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', 'Re&fresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   panes = 'Parameters' : @fm : 'Backup directory' : @fm : 'Report'
   * S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line.  The page offers the AI only what changes what is shown - its three views, the "differ from the default" row filter and refresh (an
   * administrator's page: edit and set-only are not offered); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  Where the AI is not usable nothing here adds a key or a line.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'parameters', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'backups', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'report', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'differ', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   gosub lay.declare                                            ;* the panes; VP (the parameter rows on the screen) and DV (the detail rows) come from them
   hp = '  ' : fmt('Parameter', '12L') : fmt('In force', '23L') : fmt('In sd.conf', '23L') : fmt('Default', '20L') : fmt('Takes effect', '13L') : fmt('Status', '9L') : 'Change'

   view = 1                                                     ;* 1 the parameters, 2 the backup directory, 3 the report
   pshow = '' ; nshow = 0                                       ;* the table rows shown, after the two filters
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   only.diff = 0 ; only.set = 0
   repl = '' ; rtop = 1
   conf.path = ''
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, panes<view>, '', '', mr)          ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, panes<view>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, panes<view>, nm, ao)         ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if view # 1 or only.diff or only.set then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, panes<view>, nm, busy, mr)       ;* the Esc rule: another view or a row filter is closed before the bar opens
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lay.chg)
            gosub lay.get
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* Read the table, the file and SD's own values again, and put the cursor back on the parameter it was on
read.all:
   sel.k = ''
   if nshow > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nshow then
      idx = pshow<ci>
      sel.k = pk<idx>
   end
   gosub read.table
   gosub read.file
   gosub merge.rows
   gosub filter.rows
   if sel.k # '' then
      for i = 1 to nshow
         idx = pshow<i>
         if pk<idx> = sel.k then
            ci = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   if ci > nshow then ci = nshow
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   return

* The table of parameters (sdsys/config.table): key, kind, default, min, max, effect, status, text, write, why; a line beginning # is a comment
read.table:
   tk = '' ; tkind = '' ; tdef = '' ; tmin = '' ; tmax = '' ; teff = '' ; tstat = '' ; ttext = '' ; twrite = '' ; twhy = ''
   table.err = ''
   nl = 0
   openseq @sdsys : @ds : 'config.table' readonly to tf then
      loop
         readseq ln from tf else exit
         if ln = '' or ln[1, 1] = '#' then continue
*        BY INDEX: an append with <-1> to an array that is still empty adds nothing, so a column whose first values are empty (the minimum and the maximum, blank for the first rows) slides up
*        and every later row reads the wrong range - which E would then have checked a value against (found by sandbox-tool-config.py row C8a, 26 Oct 26)
         nl += 1
         tk<nl> = field(ln, '|', 1)
         tkind<nl> = field(ln, '|', 2)
         tdef<nl> = field(ln, '|', 3)
         tmin<nl> = field(ln, '|', 4)
         tmax<nl> = field(ln, '|', 5)
         teff<nl> = field(ln, '|', 6)
         tstat<nl> = field(ln, '|', 7)
         ttext<nl> = field(ln, '|', 8)
         twrite<nl> = field(ln, '|', 9)
         twhy<nl> = field(ln, '|', 10)
      repeat
      close tf
   end else
      if not(unassigned(tf)) then close tf       ;* 26 Oct 26 - an OPENSEQ that took ELSE keeps the name locked until the variable is closed (see home_entry)
      table.err = 'the table of parameters (config.table in the system directory) cannot be read'
   end
   return

* sd.conf as SD reads it: the file the kernel read at start (SD_CONFIG, else C:\ProgramData\SD\sd.conf; K$INIPATH); lines of the [sd] section; a line KEY=value, the key in upper case, a
* line beginning # ignored.  READSEQ strips the CRLF of a Windows file.
read.file:
   fk = '' ; fv = ''
   conf.path = kernel(K$INIPATH, 0)
   file.err = ''
   section = ''
   openseq conf.path readonly to cf then
      loop
         readseq ln from cf else exit
         if ln = '' or ln[1, 1] = '#' then continue
         if ln[1, 1] = '[' then
            e = index(ln, ']', 1)
            section = upcase(ln[2, (if e > 0 then e - 2 else len(ln))])
            continue
         end
         if section # 'SD' then continue
         e = index(ln, '=', 1)
         if e = 0 then continue
         ckey = upcase(ln[1, e - 1])
         cval = ln[e + 1, len(ln)]
         gosub file.add
      repeat
      close cf
   end else
      if not(unassigned(cf)) then close cf       ;* 26 Oct 26 - as above
      file.err = conf.path : ' cannot be read'
   end
   return

* ckey and cval are one line of the file: a flag parameter that SD adds up (bits) is added up here; the others keep the last
file.add:
   p = 0
   for i = 1 to dcount(fk, @fm)
      if fk<i> = ckey then p = i
   next i
   if p = 0 then
*     26 Oct 26 (review of A6): by index, as read.table does.  Appending an EMPTY value with <-1> to an empty array adds nothing, so a first line such as SH= slid every later value up one row
      fadd.n = dcount(fk, @fm) + 1
      fk<fadd.n> = ckey
      fv<fadd.n> = cval
      return
   end
   kk = 0
   for i = 1 to dcount(tk, @fm)
      if tk<i> = ckey and tkind<i> = 'bits' then kk = 1
   next i
   old.v = fv<p>
   if kk and num(old.v) and num(cval) then
      fv<p> = bitor(old.v + 0, cval + 0)
   end else
      fv<p> = cval
   end
   return

* One row for each parameter of the table, then one for each name in the file that the table does not have; the values SD runs with, and whether the row disagrees with the file
merge.rows:
   pk = '' ; pforce = '' ; pfile = '' ; pdef = '' ; peff = '' ; pstat = '' ; ptext = '' ; prange = '' ; pdiff = '' ; pinfile = '' ; pkind = ''
   pwrite = '' ; pwhy = '' ; pmin = '' ; pmax = ''
   ndiff = 0 ; nrestart = 0 ; nin = dcount(fk, @fm) ; unknown = ''
   nt = dcount(tk, @fm)
   for i = 1 to nt
      pk<i> = tk<i>
      pkind<i> = tkind<i>
      pdef<i> = tdef<i>
      peff<i> = teff<i>
      pstat<i> = tstat<i>
      ptext<i> = ttext<i>
      pwrite<i> = twrite<i>
      pwhy<i> = twhy<i>
      pmin<i> = tmin<i>
      pmax<i> = tmax<i>
      prange<i> = (if tmin<i> = '' and tmax<i> = '' then '' else tmin<i> : ' to ' : tmax<i>)
      pforce<i> = config(tk<i>)
      if status() # 0 then pforce<i> = '(not readable)'
      p = 0
      for j = 1 to nin
         if fk<j> = tk<i> then p = j
      next j
      pinfile<i> = (p > 0)
      pfile<i> = (if p > 0 then fv<p> else '')
      pdiff<i> = 0
      if p > 0 and pforce<i> # '(not readable)' and tk<i> # 'DEBUG' then
         gosub compare.values
         if cmp.diff then
            pdiff<i> = 1
            ndiff += 1
            if teff<i> = 'restart' then nrestart += 1
         end
      end
   next i
   for j = 1 to nin
      known = 0
      for i = 1 to nt
         if tk<i> = fk<j> then known = 1
      next i
      if not(known) then
         n = dcount(pk, @fm) + 1
         pk<n> = fk<j>
         pkind<n> = '' ; pdef<n> = '' ; peff<n> = '' ; pstat<n> = 'unknown' ; prange<n> = ''
         pwrite<n> = 'no' ; pwhy<n> = 'SD does not know this name.' ; pmin<n> = '' ; pmax<n> = ''
         ptext<n> = 'SD does not know this name. SD will not start, and no new session will, while the file holds it: correct its spelling or take the line out.'
         pforce<n> = '' ; pfile<n> = fv<j> ; pinfile<n> = 1 ; pdiff<n> = 1
         unknown<-1> = fk<j>
      end
   next j
   nrows = dcount(pk, @fm)
   return

* The value in the file and the value SD runs with, for the parameter i: cmp.diff is 1 when they are different.  A number is compared as a number, a pair or a path as text.
compare.values:
   a = trim(pfile<i>)
   b = trim(pforce<i>)
   cmp.diff = (a # b)
   if cmp.diff and num(a) and num(b) then
      cmp.diff = (abs((a + 0) - (b + 0)) > 0.000000000000001)
   end
   return

* The rows shown: all, or only the rows where the file and SD disagree, or only the parameters the file sets
filter.rows:
   pshow = ''
   nshow = 0
   for i = 1 to nrows
      keep = 1
      if only.diff and not(pdiff<i>) then keep = 0
      if only.set and not(pinfile<i>) then keep = 0
      if keep then
         nshow += 1
         pshow<nshow> = i
      end
   next i
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the other two views

read.backup:
   bdir = '' ; bderr = ''
   call !acc_os_bakdir('GET', bdir, bderr)
   return

read.report:
   repl = '' ; rtop = 1
   call !settings_os(os.lines, rerr)
   if rerr # '' then
      repl = 'the report could not be made'
      return
   end
   skip = 0
   for i = 1 to dcount(os.lines, @fm)
      l = os.lines<i>
      if l[1, 1] = '[' then skip = (l[1, 9] = '[sd.conf]')
      if not(skip) then repl<-1> = l
   next i
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the layout (S.88 L2)

* The page's three boxes as panes of $tk_layout: each size is the box drawn at 140 by 43 (the body is 138 by 39), so at that size nothing moves; in a larger window the list stretches
* (a table shows more rows) and every pane is as wide as the body.  Declared again after the terminal was given away and the screen taken again.
lay.declare:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'top' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'list' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 20 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<3> = 'detail' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 13 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, lay.err)
   gosub lay.get
   return

* The rectangles of the three panes, and what is counted from them: tw the width of a text line inside a box (134 at 140 by 43), VP the parameter rows, DV the detail rows
lay.get:
   lay.id = 'top'
   gosub lay.rect
   top.x = lay.x ; top.y = lay.y ; top.w = lay.w ; top.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'list'
   gosub lay.rect
   lst.x = lay.x ; lst.y = lay.y ; lst.w = lay.w ; lst.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'detail'
   gosub lay.rect
   det.x = lay.x ; det.y = lay.y ; det.w = lay.w ; det.h = lay.h
   body.y = ctx<TK.C.YBODY>
   tx = lst.x + 2
   tw = lst.w - 4
   mk.x = top.x + top.w - 5                                     ;* the [?] button, at the right end of the first row of the top box
   mk.y = top.y + 1
   VP = lst.h - 3
   DV = det.h - 2
   return

lay.rect:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, lay.id, lay.r)
   lay.x = lay.r<1, 1>
   lay.y = lay.r<1, 2>
   lay.w = lay.r<1, 3>
   lay.h = lay.r<1, 4>
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,body.y size cw2,chh
   screen box at top.x,top.y size top.w,top.h title 'Configuration'
   ttl = 'Parameters'
   if view = 2 then ttl = 'Backup directory'
   if view = 3 then ttl = 'Report'
   screen box at lst.x,lst.y size lst.w,lst.h title ttl
   ttl = 'The parameter under the cursor'
   if view = 2 then ttl = 'About the backup directory'
   if view = 3 then ttl = 'About the report'
   screen box at det.x,det.y size det.w,det.h title ttl
   gosub draw.top
   gosub redraw
   return

draw.top:
   if table.err # '' then
      s = table.err
   end else
      if file.err # '' then
         s = file.err
      end else
         cnt.txt = '   Parameters in it: ' : nin : '   Differ from what SD is running with: ' : ndiff : '   Need a restart: ' : nrestart
*        the counts are what the administrator acts on: a long path loses its front, never the counts
         fpath = conf.path
         room = (tw - 6) - 6 - len(cnt.txt)
         if len(fpath) > room then fpath = '...' : fpath[len(fpath) - room + 4, room - 3]
         s = 'File: ' : fpath : cnt.txt
      end
   end
   screen text s[1, tw - 6] at tx,top.y + 1 attr 'bold' width tw - 6                  ;* 6 less than the other lines so that the [?] is clear
   if unknown = '' then
      s = 'Names in the file that SD does not know: none'
   end else
      s = 'NAMES IN THE FILE THAT SD DOES NOT KNOW (SD will not start with them): ' : convert(@fm, ' ', unknown)
   end
   screen text s[1, tw] at tx,top.y + 2 width tw
   screen text 'session: a change reaches the sessions started after it.  restart: it takes effect when SD is next started.   * marks a row where the file and SD disagree.' at tx,top.y + 3 width tw
   screen text 'P parameters   B backup directory   R report   D only where they disagree   S only what the file sets   E changes one   F5 reads again' at tx,top.y + 4 width tw
   call $tk_help('mark', mk.x, mk.y, 0, 0)
   return

redraw:
   begin case
      case view = 1
         gosub draw.params
         gosub draw.param.detail
      case view = 2
         gosub draw.backup
      case 1
         gosub draw.report
   end case
   return

draw.params:
   screen text hp at tx,lst.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VP then ta = ci - VP
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VP
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= nshow then
         i = pshow<kk>
         fv.s = pfile<i>
         if not(pinfile<i>) then fv.s = '-'
         fo.s = pforce<i>
         if fo.s = '' then fo.s = '(empty)'
         if pstat<i> = 'unknown' then fo.s = '-'
         df.s = pdef<i>
         if df.s = '' then df.s = '(none)'
         s = (if pdiff<i> then '* ' else '  ') : fmt(pk<i>[1, 11], '12L') : fmt(fo.s[1, 22], '23L') : fmt(fv.s[1, 22], '23L') : fmt(df.s[1, 19], '20L') : fmt(peff<i>[1, 12], '13L') : fmt(pstat<i>, '9L') : (if pwrite<i> = 'yes' then 'e' else 'by hand')
      end
      rat = 'normal'
      if kk = ci and kk <= nshow then rat = 'highlight'
      screen text s[1, tw] at tx,lst.y + 1 + r attr rat width tw
   next r
   return

* The parameter under the cursor: its facts, when a change reaches whom, and the sentence
draw.param.detail:
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text '' at tx,det.y + r width tw
   next r
   if nshow = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > nshow then
      screen text 'There is no parameter to show.' at tx,det.y + 1 width tw
      return
   end
   i = pshow<ci>
   lines = ''
   s = pk<i> : '   ' : pkind<i> : (if prange<i> = '' then '' else '   range ' : prange<i>) : '   takes effect: ' : peff<i> : '   status: ' : pstat<i>
   lines<-1> = s
   fo.s = pforce<i>
   if fo.s = '' then fo.s = '(empty)'
   s = 'SD is running with: ' : fo.s : '     sd.conf says: ' : (if pinfile<i> then pfile<i> else '(nothing)') : '     default: ' : (if pdef<i> = '' then '(none)' else pdef<i>)
   lines<-1> = s
   lines<-1> = ''
   call $tk_wrap(ptext<i>, tw, pieces)
   lines<-1> = pieces
   lines<-1> = ''
   if pwrite<i> = 'yes' then
      lines<-1> = 'E changes it here: a whole number from ' : pmin<i> : ' to ' : pmax<i> : ', the range SD itself enforces; a box shows the command first.'
   end else
      call $tk_wrap('Not changed from this page: ' : pwhy<i> : ' E shows the line to add by hand.', tw, pieces)
      lines<-1> = pieces
   end
   if pdiff<i> and pstat<i> # 'unknown' then
      lines<-1> = ''
      if peff<i> = 'restart' then
         lines<-1> = 'The file and SD disagree. This parameter takes effect only when SD is next started: until then SD keeps running with ' : fo.s : '.'
      end else
         lines<-1> = 'The file and this session disagree. Sessions started now read the file; this one, and any that were already running, keep ' : fo.s : '.'
      end
   end
   for r = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if r <= DV then
         lr = lines<r>
         screen text lr[1, tw] at tx,det.y + r width tw
      end
   next r
   return

draw.backup:
   screen text '' at tx,lst.y + 1 width tw
   for r = 1 to VP
      screen text '' at tx,lst.y + 1 + r width tw
   next r
   if bderr # '' then
      screen text 'The saved backup directory could not be read.' at tx,lst.y + 2 width tw
   end else
      if bdir = '' then
         screen text 'No backup directory has been saved. BACKUP.ACCOUNT then needs a directory typed with it, or one saved with SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY.' at tx,lst.y + 2 width tw
      end else
         screen text 'The saved backup directory (BACKUPDIR in ' : conf.path : '):' at tx,lst.y + 2 width tw
         screen text bdir[1, tw - 4] at tx + 2,lst.y + 3 attr 'bold' width tw - 4
         if ospath(bdir, OS$EXISTS) then
            screen text 'It exists.' at tx + 2,lst.y + 5 width tw - 4
         end else
            screen text 'It does not exist now. BACKUP.ACCOUNT makes it, or says why it cannot, when it next runs.' at tx + 2,lst.y + 5 width tw - 4
         end
      end
   end
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text '' at tx,det.y + r width tw
   next r
   screen text "The directory is saved with SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY, which proves it writable and writes the one line of sd.conf (BACKUPDIR) through SDSYS's elevated helper." at tx,det.y + 1 width tw
   screen text 'This page only shows it. NETFILES and SDCLIENT, which decide what an API login may reach, are on the parameters view.' at tx,det.y + 2 width tw
   return

draw.report:
   screen text 'The operating system part of SETTINGS.REPORT (the [sd.conf] section is the parameters view)' at tx,lst.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   n = dcount(repl, @fm)
   for r = 1 to VP
      kk = rtop + r - 1
      s = ''
      if kk <= n then
         s = repl<kk>
      end
      screen text s[1, tw] at tx,lst.y + 1 + r width tw
   next r
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text '' at tx,det.y + r width tw
   next r
   screen text 'Lines ' : rtop : ' to ' : (if rtop + VP - 1 > n then n else rtop + VP - 1) : ' of ' : n : '.  Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home and End scroll.  F5 makes the report again.' at tx,det.y + 1 width tw
   screen text 'It is what SETTINGS.REPORT prints for the system. It holds no key, no password hash and nothing from the credential files.' at tx,det.y + 2 width tw
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         gosub step.up
      case nm = 'down'
         gosub step.down
      case nm = 'pgup'
         for q = 1 to VP
            gosub step.up
         next q
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         for q = 1 to VP
            gosub step.down
         next q
      case nm = 'home'
         ci = 1
         rtop = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'end'
         ci = nshow
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         rtop = dcount(repl, @fm) - (VP - 1)
         if rtop < 1 then rtop = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'p'
         view = 1
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'b'
         view = 2
         gosub read.backup
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'r'
         view = 3
         gosub read.report
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'd'
         only.diff = (if only.diff then 0 else 1)
         gosub filter.rows
         ci = 1 ; ta = 0
         view = 1
         gosub draw.all
         msg = (if only.diff then 'only the rows where the file and SD disagree' else 'all the rows')
      case nm = 's'
         only.set = (if only.set then 0 else 1)
         gosub filter.rows
         ci = 1 ; ta = 0
         view = 1
         gosub draw.all
         msg = (if only.set then 'only the parameters the file sets' else 'all the rows')
      case nm = 'e'
         gosub edit.param
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, panes<view>, std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         if view = 2 then gosub read.backup
         if view = 3 then gosub read.report
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read again'
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.config.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here: the view shown) and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
      case nm = 'esc'
         if view # 1 or only.diff or only.set then
            if only.diff or only.set then
               only.diff = 0 ; only.set = 0
               gosub filter.rows
               ci = 1 ; ta = 0                                ;* the rows changed: the cursor goes to the top; leaving the Backup or Report view alone keeps it where it was
            end
            view = 1
            gosub draw.all
         end
   end case
   return

step.up:
   if view = 1 then
      if ci > 1 then ci -= 1
   end
   if view = 3 then
      if rtop > 1 then rtop -= 1
   end
   gosub redraw
   return

step.down:
   if view = 1 then
      if ci < nshow then ci += 1
   end
   if view = 3 then
      if rtop + VP - 1 < dcount(repl, @fm) then rtop += 1
   end
   gosub redraw
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, panes<view>, mev, '', mr)                 ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, panes<view>, mev, ap)                        ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mk.x, mk.y, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.config.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if view = 1 and mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= tx and mx <= tx + tw - 1 and my >= lst.y + 2 and my <= lst.y + 1 + VP then
         if ta + my - (lst.y + 1) <= nshow then
            ci = ta + my - (lst.y + 1)
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the one change this page can make

* E on the parameter under the cursor: a parameter the table marks write=yes is changed (change.param); any other is explained (explain.fixed) and nothing is written
edit.param:
   if view # 1 then
      msg = 'E changes a parameter: press P for the parameters first'
      return
   end
   if nshow = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > nshow then
      msg = 'there is no parameter to change'
      return
   end
   i = pshow<ci>
   k = pk<i>
   if pwrite<i> = 'yes' then
      gosub change.param
   end else
      gosub explain.fixed
   end
   return

* Not changed here: the reason from the table and the exact line to add by hand (as an administrator, in the file SD reads), and when it would take effect.  This writes nothing and runs nothing.
explain.fixed:
   body = k : ' is not changed from this page.'
   body<-1> = ''
   if pstat<i> = 'unknown' then
      call $tk_wrap('SD does not know this name, and SD will not start, and no new session will, while the file holds it. Take the line out of ' : conf.path : ' by hand, as an administrator, or correct its spelling.', 100, pieces)
      body<-1> = pieces
   end else
      call $tk_wrap('Why: ' : pwhy<i>, 100, pieces)
      body<-1> = pieces
      body<-1> = ''
      call $tk_wrap('To change it, as an administrator, put the line ' : k : '=<value> in the [sd] section of ' : conf.path : ' (the default is ' : (if pdef<i> = '' then 'none' else pdef<i>) : ').', 100, pieces)
      body<-1> = pieces
      begin case
         case peff<i> = 'restart'
            wh = 'It takes effect when SD is next stopped and started (sd -restart, or Stop-Service SD then Start-Service SD).'
         case peff<i> = 'session'
            wh = 'Sessions started after the edit read it; sessions already running keep the old value.'
         case 1
            wh = 'It takes effect at once, wherever the file is read.'
      end case
      call $tk_wrap(wh : ' A value SD does not accept stops SD, and every new session, from starting: read the guide first.', 100, pieces)
      body<-1> = pieces
   end
   screen msgbox body title 'Not changed here' buttons '&Close' default 1 returning bx else bx = 0
   msg = k : ' is not changed from this page; nothing was written'
   return

* A parameter set.config may change: ask for the value, check it against the table, show the command in the toolkit's box, run it, read everything again and say what changed.  The value
* is digits only and the name is the table's, so $tk_run's character rules are never the only thing between a keystroke and the command line.
change.param:
   fo = pforce<i>
   if fo = '' then fo = '(empty)'
   old.f = (if pinfile<i> then pfile<i> else '(nothing)')
   qq = 'New value for ' : k : ': a whole number from ' : pmin<i> : ' to ' : pmax<i> : ' (SD runs with ' : fo : ', sd.conf says ' : old.f : ')'
   tt = 'Change ' : k
   nv = ''
   k.eff = peff<i>                                              ;* kept: read.all below reuses the loop variable i
   screen ask qq width 12 value '' title tt returning nv then got = 1 else got = 0
   if not(got) then
      msg = 'canceled; ' : k : ' is unchanged'
      return
   end
   nv = trim(nv)
   if nv = '' then
      msg = 'nothing was typed; ' : k : ' is unchanged'
      return
   end
   ok = (len(nv) <= 7)
   for q = 1 to len(nv)
      if index('0123456789', nv[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = @false
   next q
   if ok then ok = (('S' : nv) = 'S0' or nv[1, 1] # '0')
   if ok then ok = ((nv + 0) >= (pmin<i> + 0) and (nv + 0) <= (pmax<i> + 0))
   if not(ok) then
      msg = k : ' takes a whole number from ' : pmin<i> : ' to ' : pmax<i> : ', digits only; nothing was changed'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.config ' : downcase(k) : ' ' : nv
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'Sets ' : k : ' to ' : nv : ' in ' : conf.path : ' (now ' : old.f : '; the default is ' : (if pdef<i> = '' then 'none' else pdef<i>) : '). The line is replaced where it is, every other line is kept, and the file as it is now is kept as sd.conf.bak.'
   if env('SD_CONFIG') # '' then
      el<-1> = 'This session reads ' : conf.path : ' (SD_CONFIG), but the elevated helper changes the sd.conf in ProgramData\SD only.'
   end
   if peff<i> = 'restart' then
      el<-1> = 'It takes effect when SD is next stopped and started (sd -restart, or Stop-Service SD then Start-Service SD). Until then SD, and every session, keeps running with ' : fo : '.'
   end else
      el<-1> = 'Sessions started after this read the new value. This session, and any that are already running, keep ' : fo : '.'
   end
   el<-1> = "SDSYS's elevated helper makes the change and the verb writes one line to the audit trail."
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   if err # '' then
      msg = err
      return
   end
*  What the disk and SD say now, not what the verb said: the row of this parameter, found again
   rj = 0
   for j = 1 to nrows
      if pk<j> = k then rj = j
   next j
   now.f = (if rj > 0 and pinfile<rj> then pfile<rj> else '(nothing)')
   now.r = (if rj > 0 then pforce<rj> else '')
   lastl = ''
   for j = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
      if trim(out<j>) # '' then lastl = trim(out<j>)
   next j
   if stat = 0 and ('S' : trim(now.f)) = ('S' : nv) then
      msg = k : ' in sd.conf: ' : old.f : ' -> ' : now.f : '; SD is running with ' : now.r : (if k.eff = 'restart' then ' until it is restarted' else ' (sessions started now use ' : now.f : ')')
   end else
      msg = 'sd.conf was not changed' : (if lastl = '' then '' else ': ' : lastl)
   end
   return

end

